HST Office: Explorer preview pane and thumbnails for PDF files, rendered with the office's own PDFium.

hstpdfpreview.dll (program\shlxthdl, next to the other Explorer extensions, in the optional "Windows
Explorer extensions" feature) implements a preview handler (IPreviewHandler, run by the shell in
prevhost.exe: every page fitted to the pane width, scrolled with the scroll bar, wheel and keyboard,
following the pane's colours) and a thumbnail provider (IThumbnailProvider: the first page; the shell
runs stream-initialised providers in an isolated surrogate). Both read the file through the shell's
IStream and load program\pdfiumlo.dll at run time, so no office process starts and nothing new is
shipped besides the small DLL.

Registration never takes over another PDF program's preview: the handlers are set on HST Office's own
ProgID HSTOffice.Pdf (consulted only while the user's PDF app is HST Office) and, as a fallback, in
SystemFileAssociations\.pdf\ShellEx, which the shell consults last. A fallback value is written only
when AppSearch found that slot empty or already HST's, so another program's value is neither replaced
nor removed at uninstall. .pdf\ShellEx (e.g. Edge's "Microsoft PDF Previewer") is not touched.

